    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d516">

                <pb facs="0598" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">339.115 General Motors Export Co./184:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-29T18:00:00-05:00">May 29, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. My despatches number 2483 and number 2510, May 10 and 18.<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d516-f1"/> Court of Appeals today reversed decision of lower court
                    which imposed fine of $2,000 on Dominican Tobacco Company, condemned company to
                    penalty of 2 years imprisonment in the person of its president and to pay costs
                    of proceeding.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
